-- title:
--   Proposition 5.5 — $K|\psi\rangle^{\otimes2}=0$ iff $\psi$ is a Slater determinant
-- statement:
--   Let $G=\sum_{j=1}^n c_j\otimes c_j^\dagger$ and $K=G^\dagger G$. A state $|\psi\rangle$ of the $n$-mode fermionic Fock space obeys
--
--   $$
--   K|\psi\rangle^{\otimes2}=0
--   $$
--
--   if and only if $|\psi\rangle$ is a Slater determinant. The state is arbitrary: it need not have definite parity or particle number.
--
--   This is the perfect completeness of the two-copy Slater tester, and the converse needed by Theorem 3.5.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the fermionic Fock space ⋀ℂⁿ and the bosonic Fock space ⋁ℂⁿ → ℓ²(Fin n → Fin 2) (Jordan–Wigner, 1 = occupied, 0-based modes) and ℓ²(Fin n → ℕ); ℋ^{⊗k} is ℓ²(Fin k → ι); reason: unitarily the same spaces; Lean convention
--   - encoding: classes of pure states (rays) → sets of unit vectors closed under global phase (Coh_n gets an explicit e^{iθ}, G_f an explicit phase in its orbit); reason: dist(ψ, 𝒞) is phase-invariant, so no distance changes
--   - encoding: fermionic Gaussian unitaries, generated by Hamiltonians quadratic in c, c† (p.17) → finite products exp(A₁)⋯exp(A_L) with A_l = ¼ Σ_{p,q} h⁽ˡ⁾_{pq} γ_p γ_q, h⁽ˡ⁾ real antisymmetric (Gf, Slater ⊆ Gf); reason: a Hermitian quadratic Hamiltonian is (i/4) Σ h_{pq} γ_p γ_q + c·I with h real antisymmetric, so the group it generates is exactly these products up to the phase e^{−ic}
--   - encoding: the two-copy space ⋀ℂⁿ ⊗ ⋀ℂⁿ and the two-copy operators A ⊗ B of (4.1) and Definition 5.2 → Kronecker products of the Jordan–Wigner matrices on Fin 2 → (Fin n → Fin 2) (kron2, copy 0 = first factor); reason: the paper's ⊗ is the ungraded tensor product (Lemma 5.15 decomposes ⋀ℂⁿ ⊗ ⋀ℂⁿ = ⊕ H_a ⊗ H_b; the proof of Proposition 5.5 factors ⟨Ψ|G†G|Ψ⟩ copy by copy)
-- source:
--   Iyer, O'Gorman, Parekh, Thompson, Zhao, Optimal testing of fermionic and bosonic Gaussian states, arXiv:2609.39113 (sha256 6683e57b…), Proposition 5.5, p.42; Definition 5.2, p.41

import Definitions.Def_GaussTesting_Slater
import Definitions.Def_GaussTesting_testSlater
import Definitions.Def_GaussTesting_tpow

namespace GaussTesting

/-- **Proposition 5.5.** A state `|ψ⟩` obeys `K |ψ⟩^{⊗2} = 0` if and only if `|ψ⟩` is a Slater
determinant.

Source: Iyer, O'Gorman, Parekh, Thompson, Zhao, *Optimal testing of fermionic and bosonic Gaussian states*, arXiv:2609.39113 (sha256 6683e57b…), Proposition 5.5, p.42; `K = G†G`, `G = ∑ⱼ cⱼ ⊗ cⱼ†` (Definition 5.2, p.41).

**Formalization Note.** "A state" is any unit vector of the full fermionic Fock space `⋀ℂⁿ`, of any
parity and of indefinite particle number. -/
theorem proposition_5_5 (n : ℕ) (ψ : Ell2 (FermiCap.Gaussian.Qubits n)) (hψ : ‖ψ‖ = 1) :
    (kOp n).mulVec (fun x => tpow 2 ψ x) = 0 ↔ ψ ∈ Slater n := by sorry

end GaussTesting
